{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/718788-changeling-wuxia-o","id":718788,"title":"Changeling Wuxia?? :O","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-23T06:30:29-07:00","id":718788,"title":"Changeling Wuxia?? :O","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Ok, so the book Dark Eras is almost upon us, and one of the eras for Changeling (and Geist) will be Three Kingdom China. I imagine it will be a very cool and evocative setting, but probably, like all the other Dark Eras settings, will be more &quot;realistic&quot;.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Which is cool and all, but it would be awesome (to me, at least) if not only the setting was different from the norm, but some of the rules as well. Not only changeling the setting, but the whole genre!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">So, if not covered by the rules of the Dark Eras chapter, I would try a bit of a Changeling Wuxia. These are my adaptations for it to be possible:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- First, as it would be a chronicle with a good amount of combat, I don\u2019t want my players feeling like they have to create only physical characters. So, during a Wuxia battle, you can use any Power attribute (Strength, Intelligence, Charisma) instead of just strength. Or, with fighting finesse, any Finesse attribute (Dexterity, Manipulation, Wits).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- Also, A Wuxia artist can fight rolling Performance and Academics instead of Melee or Brawl. Or should Wuxia be a new Skill?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- A Wuxia artist jumps automatically = Main Power Stat + Athletics in Meters.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- A Wuxia artist has great balance, always.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- A Wuxia artist is made of chocolate.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- Your Weight is equal to you size x2 in kg. So a size 5 character can stand on top of a bamboo tree. A size 6 cannot (Totally convinced you I did this math, but I don\u2019t know how much weight a bamboo tree can stand).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- Also, I will be adapting the rules from Exalted\u2019s Burn Legend, in some form. Mostly the battle cards. Attributes, Skills and Merits will follow the regular game. Burn Legend uses cards with fighting techniques, and a different health system.<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you guys think? Anything to add?</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T07:09:57-07:00","id":718902,"title":"","content":"sounds pretty cool. maybe look up some martial art forms from the time period and write up a couple specific rules for them. i think white crane existed at the time, maybe changelings with that can inflict blinded tilts and make some attacks while grappled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7141-nasrudin","name":"Nasrudin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T07:32:48-07:00","id":719028,"title":"","content":"I'm not against rules hacks like this (<i>Dudes of Legend </i>is one of the best NWoD products ever released) but if they made the only Chinese era in <i>Dark Eras</i> wuxia, that'd be some &quot;romanticisation of the Other&quot; to a really uncomfortable degree. Like, 90s White Wolf uncomfortable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T09:45:10-07:00","id":719667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/718788-changeling-wuxia-o?p=719028#post719028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not against rules hacks like this (<i>Dudes of Legend </i>is one of the best NWoD products ever released) but if they made the only Chinese era in <i>Dark Eras</i> wuxia, that'd be some &quot;romanticisation of the Other&quot; to a really uncomfortable degree. Like, 90s White Wolf uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm pretty sure they won't do this, because all the other eras are realistic settings. At most a sidebar with a hack for fans of the genre. Also, I don't think it's romanticisation or anything like that, because that's trying to emulate a genre, not saying that every asian Changeling go by this rule. I think both are very different ideas. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nasrudin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/718788-changeling-wuxia-o?p=718902#post718902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sounds pretty cool. maybe look up some martial art forms from the time period and write up a couple specific rules for them. i think white crane existed at the time, maybe changelings with that can inflict blinded tilts and make some attacks while grappled?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. That is a good idea, because different schools will have different flavors. So far I only plan on using the Burn Legends stuff, and use every Exalted type's art as whatever is closer to the dynamic of the character. Only because that's less work for me. Hahah.<br /> <br /> I think, in this setting, mostly supernatural splats will be Wuxia artists. Maybe Hunters as well.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T12:11:33-07:00","id":720104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/718788-changeling-wuxia-o?p=719667#post719667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think, in this setting, mostly supernatural splats will be Wuxia artists. Maybe Hunters as well.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That'd definitely fit. Makes me think of The Matrix. Supernaturals would be like your Agents and the programs, Hunters would be the resistance fighters.<br /> <br /> There are a couple of supernatural-specific fighting styles written up in Vampire 2E and Werewolf 2E. I bet <i>The Hurt Locker</i> will help out when it finally drops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T12:23:33-07:00","id":720141,"title":"","content":"Realism is up for grabs when one of the main historical sources on the period is the reference basis of Dynasty Warriors &amp; Weapons of the Gods - for a game about past eras of a world where monsters hiding amidst human society is the norm.<br /> <br /> And gothic literature is romantic too and it doesn't make the vampires any less lethal or scary because of that. Monsters that feel and love don't stop being monsters and some pretty good wuxia films exist that play up exactly with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-23-2015, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T12:30:54-07:00","id":720185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/718788-changeling-wuxia-o?p=720141#post720141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Realism is up for grabs when one of the main historical sources on the period is the reference basis of Dynasty Warriors &amp; Weapons of the Gods - for a game about past eras of a world where monsters hiding amidst human society is the norm.<br /> <br /> And gothic literature is romantic too and it doesn't make the vampires any less lethal or scary because of that. Monsters that feel and love don't stop being monsters and some pretty good wuxia films exist that play up exactly with this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Realism has nothing to do with it. It was the &quot;Let's make the Chinese setting different because wuxia is Chinese&quot; part that bothered me. Now that I know the OP wasn't suggesting that the official era to be the new <i>Demon Hunter X</i> because China, it doesn't bother me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T10:17:33-07:00","id":723514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/718788-changeling-wuxia-o?p=720185#post720185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Realism has nothing to do with it. It was the &quot;Let's make the Chinese setting different because wuxia is Chinese&quot; part that bothered me. Now that I know the OP wasn't suggesting that the official era to be the new <i>Demon Hunter X</i> because China, it doesn't bother me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, it <b>is </b>a period of chinese history that basically screams &quot;wuxia&quot;, unlike the Republic of China in the first half of the 20th century for example, that kind of calls for something between Pulp and Noir, with japanese occupation resonating with <i>La Resistance</i> tropes, depending on how one looks at it, at least imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T11:06:49-07:00","id":723646,"title":"","content":"The Dark Eras are written with realism in mind, aiming to create a believable(not accurate) stage piece for players to roam around in and take part in. Wuxia is not particularly in line with that...but this is a game where you'll be playing as shen, more or less. Common magical powers available to changelings and sin-eaters can lead to a wuxia style game.<br /> <br /> On the mentality behind this decision, I suppose the big question is, genre appeal asides, why are you doing this? Could a modern game of China or America have these same rules? I know in my write up for Paris, I designed duels in such a way that could evoke the image, though not the gameplay, of soft wuxia, and it's one of those things I want to tweak because I want more of that soft-wuxia/semi-dream like evocation. You should figure out why you want Wuxia, and what that means for your world and gameplay and how that reflects on the real world's relationship to the style.<br /> <br /> I suppose the real question is what aspect are you wanting to bring in the most. Do you want an Exalted 3rd style of building an advantage and then striking a killing blow, or are you more concerned with the movement and flow, increasing and allowing for more three dimensional battles?<br /> <br /> Either way, I would actually posit that there's a set of in-game rules that changelings and sin-eaters can invoke if you want to bring in wuxia, and the best way to do that is to imply that the events going on in China are either bringing down Arcadian/Dead Dominion laws, or that the inverse is true and the weird as hell laws being brought down is part of what's pushing the problems in the first place. Either way, making a plasm/glamour payment to engage a substrata of reality seems like a good start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T09:24:20-07:00","id":726296,"title":"","content":"I don't understand how your adaptations even begin to capture wuxia. You're trying to emulate wire-fu, not wuxia. They're two very different things. I mean, you're basically saying that you'll do Arthurian by having plate armor and lances.<br /> <br /> The bit about chocolate is true, though. Turns out, Arcadia is actually in the Amazon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:14:12-07:00","id":726710,"title":"","content":"Actually, divorcing the idea from wuxia specifically isn't a bad idea, really.<br /> <br /> I mean if memory serves European myths and legends have included feats like killing 300 men with one sword maneuver, or running across thrown spears or arrows in flight (I don't remember which).<br /> <br /> There could be a changeling martial art dating back to Scathach's school.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T17:03:01-07:00","id":727390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/718788-changeling-wuxia-o#post718788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Ok, so the book Dark Eras is almost upon us, and one of the eras for Changeling (and Geist) will be Three Kingdom China. I imagine it will be a very cool and evocative setting, but probably, like all the other Dark Eras settings, will be more &amp;quot;realistic&amp;quot;.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Which is cool and all, but it would be awesome (to me, at least) if not only the setting was different from the norm, but some of the rules as well. Not only changeling the setting, but the whole genre!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">So, if not covered by the rules of the Dark Eras chapter, I would try a bit of a Changeling Wuxia. These are my adaptations for it to be possible:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- First, as it would be a chronicle with a good amount of combat, I don\u2019t want my players feeling like they have to create only physical characters. So, during a Wuxia battle, you can use any Power attribute (Strength, Intelligence, Charisma) instead of just strength. Or, with fighting finesse, any Finesse attribute (Dexterity, Manipulation, Wits).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- Also, A Wuxia artist can fight rolling Performance and Academics instead of Melee or Brawl. Or should Wuxia be a new Skill?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- A Wuxia artist jumps automatically = Main Power Stat + Athletics in Meters.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- A Wuxia artist has great balance, always.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- A Wuxia artist is made of chocolate.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- Your Weight is equal to you size x2 in kg. So a size 5 character can stand on top of a bamboo tree. A size 6 cannot (Totally convinced you I did this math, but I don\u2019t know how much weight a bamboo tree can stand).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">- Also, I will be adapting the rules from Exalted\u2019s Burn Legend, in some form. Mostly the battle cards. Attributes, Skills and Merits will follow the regular game. Burn Legend uses cards with fighting techniques, and a different health system.<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you guys think? Anything to add?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Others have already remarked on the mechanics of what you want to do. I'd like to clarify your terminology. You say wuxia, but I think you mean wushu. <br /> <br /> Wushu = kind of Chinese martial art<br /> <br /> Wuxia = kind of Chinese martial arts fiction.<br /> <br /> For instance, kongfu and wushu are both martial arts. The first is famous for its relationship with Buddhist monasteries. The second is taught to members of the Chinese armed forces.<br /> <br /> The film (and the novel) Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon is an example of a wuxia story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T10:49:49-07:00","id":729320,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my hack is for Wire-Fu. Which would be a tool to create a Wuxia story. <br /> <br /> But I shouldn't have said Wuxia artist, that's completely wrong. Since I was 15 I completely associate wuxia as any style in a wuxia story. Which term you guys think would be more accurate? Martial Artist? Fighter? Shen?<br /> <br /> And answering ArcaneArts, why I'm doing this? Because when I told my players about this era, one of them made the connection to Wuxia, and I thought it would be fun to consider it. We only play WoD, so we haven't tried different genres besides terror. And my group references to ancient China are mostly Wuxia wire-fu movies.<br /> <br /> So, the game would be in the genre, but let's say the same character pops up in another chronicle. He would just be a very competent martial artist.<br /> <br /> But I guess it's better to expect to see what's in the Dark Era. It might have a canon power or two that mildly evokes the feeling of wire-fu without flipping the genre. Like Victorian Lost had powers to dissipate in the london fog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T20:30:37-07:00","id":736667,"title":"","content":"Martial artist is fine but keep in mind that monks, philosophers, and soldiers are also people that commonly master wushu. IIRC &quot;wushu&quot; actually refers to the martial arts specifically in the military context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T21:04:54-07:00","id":736757,"title":"","content":"I may be misled about this, but it seems you are going for the cinematic route. Regardless of Era, I do like the idea of letting changelings spend Glamour points to boost Finesse Attributes like vampires boost Physical Attributes (1 point gives +2, and you can spend as many Glamour points as your Wyrd allows this turn). Along with that, all characters have Fighting Finesse for any weapons you deem acceptable. You could homebrew an alternate Fighting Finesse that uses Wits instead of Dexterity. Both of these Merits can be used in conjunction with Glamour to boost your Brawl, Weaponry and Athletics dice pools. Defensive Combat (Brawl and Weaponry) would be available on demand, like Fighting Finesse. Jumping would be like the Vigor of vampires: you jump a number of meters equal to (successes on the Dexterity + Athletics roll) x (Wyrd + 1). You could have Hedgespun versions of the outfits and weapons of era. You could make up a Wuxia Fighting Style based on evasion, disarming and counterattacks. Lastly, a Pledge based on the code of <i>xia</i> or another code of honor would be fitting.<br /> <br /> Sorry if I said anything that doesn't fit with the time period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T22:57:24-07:00","id":737029,"title":"","content":"I would think the easiest way to do it would be with a set of contracts. One dot: Run up vertical surfaces (yes, I know this one already exists but in a different group), Second dot: Jump higher, Third dot: Run on less than solid surfaces (like water) and Fourth dot: Run on the wind or other less substantial material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}